  "job_B3.3.17.3_20251003_114702": {
    "text": "De Sancto Martino Confessore..\nMen \u00fea leofestan, magon we nu hwylcumhwego wordum asecgan be \u00fe\u00e6re arwyr\u00f0nesse \u00feysse halgan\nW\u00e6s he Gode swi\u00f0e gecoren on his \u00feeawum.\nW\u00e6s he in Pannana \u00fe\u00e6re m\u00e6g\u00f0e in woruld cumen, in Arrea \u00f0am tune.\nW\u00e6s he hw\u00e6\u00f0re in Italia afeded, in Ticinan \u00fe\u00e6re byrig.\nW\u00e6s he for worulde swi\u00f0e godre gebyrde.\nW\u00e6ron his f\u00e6der & his modor buta h\u00e6\u00f0en.\nW\u00e6s his f\u00e6der \u00e6rest cyninges \u00feegn, & \u00fea \u00e6t nehstan ge\u00feah \u00fe\u00e6t he w\u00e6s tribunus, \u00fe\u00e6t is ealdorman\n\u00dea sceolde he, sanctus Martinus, nyde beon sona on his giogo\u00f0hade on geferr\u00e6ddenne cyninges \u00feegna,\nNalles \u00fe\u00e6t he his on \u00feam willan on \u00feam woruldfolgo\u00f0e w\u00e6re, ac he w\u00e6s on Godes \u00feeowdome mycle\n& \u00fea he w\u00e6s X wintre, \u00fea tihton hine his yldran to woruldfolgo\u00f0e, & \u00fea fleah he to Godes cirican &\n\u00dea he w\u00e6s XV wintra, \u00fea genyddon hie hine, his yldran, to \u00fean \u00fe\u00e6t he sceolde w\u00e6pnum onfon, & on\n\u00d0a w\u00e6ron \u00fereo gear \u00e6r his fulwihte \u00fe\u00e6t he woruldlicu w\u00e6pen w\u00e6g.\n& he hine hw\u00e6\u00f0re wi\u00f0 eallum \u00feam healicum synnum geheold, \u00fea \u00f0e woruldmen fremmia\u00f0 in\nH\u00e6fde he mycle lufan & ealle swetnesse to \u00e6lcum men, & he w\u00e6s ge\u00feyldig & eadmod & gemetf\u00e6st on\n& \u00feeah \u00fee he gyt on l\u00e6wedum hade beon sceolde, & hw\u00e6\u00f0re he to \u00fe\u00e6s mycle forh\u00e6fdnesse h\u00e6fde on\nW\u00e6s he for his arf\u00e6stum d\u00e6dum eallum his geferum leof & wyr\u00f0 & ondrysne, & hie hine ealle mid\n& \u00feeah \u00f0e he \u00fea gyt ne w\u00e6re fullice \u00e6fter cierican endebyrdnesse gefullad, ac he w\u00e6s gecristnod, swa\nHe wolde \u00feam winnendum fultumian, & earme frefran, & hingriendum mete syllan, & nacode scrydan.\n& eall \u00f0\u00e6t he on his folgo\u00f0e begeat, eall \u00fe\u00e6t he for Gode sealde butan \u00fe\u00e6re d\u00e6ghw\u00e6mlican andlyfne\nGemunde he \u00fe\u00e6t Godes bebod \u00fe\u00e6t he sylfa on his godspelle bebead: he swa cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t se Godes man\nMen \u00fea leofestan, magon we nu \u00feara arf\u00e6stra d\u00e6da sume asecgan \u00f0e \u00f0es eadiga wer sanctus Martinus\nHe sona in cnihthade gedyde, \u00feeah \u00feara godra d\u00e6da ma w\u00e6re \u00feonne hit \u00e6nig man asecgan m\u00e6ge.\n& \u00fe\u00e6t gelamp sume si\u00f0e \u00fe\u00e6t he ferde mid o\u00f0rum cyninges \u00feegnum in \u00fea burh \u00fee Ambinensis hatte.\nW\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6t in midda wintra.\nW\u00e6s se winter \u00fey geare to \u00fe\u00e6s grim \u00fe\u00e6t efne manige men w\u00e6ron \u00fe\u00e6t heora feorh for cyle gesealdan.\n\u00dea s\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6r sum \u00feearfa \u00e6t \u00f0am burggeate wel neah \u00f0on, & se nacoda b\u00e6d him \u00fea for Gode hr\u00e6gles on\n\u00dea ferdon hie ealle for\u00f0 be him, & heora n\u00e6nig to him gecyrran nolde, ne him \u00e6nige are gedon woldon.\n\u00dea ongeat he, se Godes man, \u00fe\u00e6t drihten him \u00feone \u00feearfendan man geheold \u00fe\u00e6t he him miltsian\nNyste \u00fea hw\u00e6\u00f0re hw\u00e6t he him don sceolde, for \u00fean \u00fee he nowiht elles h\u00e6fde butan his anfealdne\nGeteah \u00fea his seax, & genam his sciccels \u00feone his lodan \u00fee he him on h\u00e6fde.\nSna\u00f0 \u00fea \u00feone in tu, & \u00fea healfne \u00feam \u00feearfan sealde & mid healfe hine eft besweop.\n\u00dea w\u00e6ron manige men \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6t gesawon \u00fe\u00e6t hie hine on \u00feam t\u00e6ldon & besmyredon, \u00fe\u00e6t he swa his\nSume \u00feonne eft, \u00f0a \u00f0e beteran modes w\u00e6ron & \u00e6nige lufan to Gode h\u00e6fdon, hie sylfe on \u00feon oncu\u00f0on\n& \u00fea w\u00e6s in \u00fe\u00e6re \u00e6fterfylgendan niht \u00f0a \u00fees eadiga wer slepte, & \u00fea geseah he Crist sylfne mid \u00fey\n& \u00fea w\u00e6s him beboden geornlicor \u00fe\u00e6t he hine, dryhten, ongeate & \u00fe\u00e6t hr\u00e6gl \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00e6r \u00feam \u00feearfan\nMartinus nu iu, he cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00feus, gecristnod \u00e6r his fulwihte, he mid \u00feysse hr\u00e6gle me gegyrede.\nW\u00e6s in \u00fe\u00e6re d\u00e6de sweotol \u00f0\u00e6t ure dryhten is swi\u00f0e gemyndig \u00fe\u00e6s cwides \u00fee he sylfa \u00e6r cw\u00e6\u00f0: Swa\nHe \u00f0a wolde \u00feone cwide gefyllan in \u00fe\u00e6re godan d\u00e6de, & hine sylfne geea\u00f0medde to \u00fe\u00e6n \u00fe\u00e6t he wolde\n& \u00f0a se eadiga wer sanctus Martinus \u00f0a gesyh\u00f0e geseah, \u00fea ne w\u00e6s he hw\u00e6\u00f0re oht ofor \u00fean in\n\u00d0a he \u00f0a h\u00e6fde eahtatyne wintra, \u00f0a gefullade hine man \u00e6fter cirican endebyrdnesse.\nW\u00e6s he \u00e6r beforan \u00fea \u00fereo gear gecristnod, swa ic \u00e6r s\u00e6gde.\n\u00d0a forlet he ealne \u00feone woruldfolgo\u00f0 an, & \u00f0a gewat he to sancte Ilario \u00feam bisceope, \u00fee in\nW\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6t swi\u00f0e forem\u00e6re man, se bisceop, & his god w\u00e6s swi\u00f0e gecy\u00f0ed.\n& he \u00fea \u00feysne eadigan wer sancte Martine fulfremedlice in Godes \u00e6 & in Godes \u00feeowdome getyde &\nW\u00e6s he swi\u00f0e ge\u00feungen on his \u00feeawum, & gest\u00e6\u00f0\u00f0ig on his wordum, & hluttor & \u00e6rf\u00e6st & cl\u00e6ne on\n& \u00fea gelamp \u00e6fter \u00fean \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fees eadiga wer sanctus Martinus sum mynster him getimbrade, & he on\n& \u00fea gelamp sume si\u00f0e \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6r cwom sum gecristnod man to him \u00fe\u00e6t he wolde mid his lare & mid his\n& \u00fea he \u00f0a \u00fe\u00e6r w\u00e6s wel manige dagas, \u00fea wear\u00f0 he untrum, se man, in \u00fe\u00e6re feferadle.\n& \u00fea gelamp in \u00f0a tid \u00fe\u00e6t he, sanctus Martinus, w\u00e6s in sumre fore ealle dogor.\n\u00dea he \u00f0a eft ham cwom, \u00fea mette he \u00feone man for\u00f0feredne \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6r \u00e6r untrum w\u00e6s, & hine efne swa\n\u00d0a he \u00f0a, sanctus Martinus, \u00fe\u00e6t geseah \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fea o\u00f0re bro\u00f0or ealle swa unrote leton ymbe \u00fe\u00e6t lic, & hie\nW\u00e6s him \u00fe\u00e6t swi\u00f0e mycle weorce \u00fe\u00e6t he swa ungefullad for\u00f0feran sceolde.\nGetreowde hine \u00f0a hw\u00e6\u00f0re on \u00feone \u00e6lmihtigan Gode mid ealle mode & on his mildheortnesse.\nEode he \u00f0a hw\u00e6\u00f0re in \u00fe\u00e6t hus \u00fe\u00e6r se lichama inne l\u00e6g, & het \u00fea o\u00f0re men ealle ut gangan, & he \u00f0a\n\u00d0a he \u00f0a lange hwile swa in \u00feam gebede w\u00e6s, \u00f0a ongeat he \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6r w\u00e6s godcund m\u00e6gn andweard,\n\u00dea w\u00e6s ymbe hwile \u00fea gefylde he his lare lufian, for \u00fean he swa cu\u00f0e & Godes gife on him w\u00e6s & his\n& he manig tempel & deofulgild gebr\u00e6c & gefylde, & he \u00feonne \u00fe\u00e6r asette Godes cirican, o\u00f0\u00f0e fullice\n& \u00fe\u00e6t gelamp sume si\u00f0e eac \u00fe\u00e6t he ongan onb\u00e6rnan sum deofolgild \u00fe\u00e6t mid \u00feam h\u00e6\u00f0enum mannum\n\u00dea stod \u00fe\u00e6r sum nyttwyr\u00f0e hus bi \u00f0am h\u00e6\u00f0engilde \u00fee he \u00fe\u00e6r b\u00e6rnan ongan.\n\u00dea slog se wind \u00feone lig on \u00fe\u00e6t nyttwyr\u00f0e hus, & him \u00feuhte \u00fe\u00e6t hit eall forb\u00e6rnan sceolde.\n\u00dea he \u00f0a, sanctus Martinus, \u00fe\u00e6t geseah, \u00fea arn he sona up on \u00fe\u00e6t hus, & gestod he ongen \u00feam lige.\n\u00dea gelamp wundorlice wyrd, \u00fe\u00e6t se lig ongan slean & brecan ongen \u00feam winde, & efne swa swa se\n& swa w\u00e6s \u00fea se lig ge\u00fereatod \u00feurh sancte Martines gebedu, \u00fe\u00e6t he n\u00e6nigum o\u00f0rum \u00feingum ne\nSwylce gelamp o\u00f0er wundor \u00feyssum onlic.\nHe cwom to sumum tune \u00fee Libras w\u00e6s haten.\n\u00dea w\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6r sum diofolgild \u00fee \u00f0a h\u00e6\u00f0enan men godgild heton, & hie hine swi\u00f0e weor\u00f0edon.\n\u00d0a wolde sanctus Martinus \u00e6lce \u00feinge \u00fe\u00e6t gild tobrecan & gefyllan.\n\u00dea wi\u00f0stodon him \u00fea h\u00e6\u00f0enan men, & hie hine mid teonum aweg adrifon.\n\u00d0a eode he \u00f0\u00e6rrihte bii in sume stowe, & he hine gegyrede mid h\u00e6rene hr\u00e6gle swi\u00f0e hearde & swi\u00f0e\n& \u00fea cwomon \u00fe\u00e6r semninga twegen englas to him, gescildode & gesweordode & mid heregeatwum\n\u00dea eodon hie eft to \u00feam tune & \u00fe\u00e6t deofulgild tobr\u00e6con & gefyldon aa o\u00f0 grund.\n& \u00fea h\u00e6\u00f0enan men tolocedon, & hie hw\u00e6\u00f0re w\u00e6ron mid \u00fey godcundan m\u00e6gene to \u00fe\u00e6s swi\u00f0e\nAc hie ealle to dryhtnes geleafan gecyrdon, & hie swa cw\u00e6don \u00fe\u00e6t w\u00e6re so\u00f0 God se \u00f0e Martine\nSwylce eac gelamp sume si\u00f0e \u00fe\u00e6r he sum h\u00e6\u00f0engild gebr\u00e6c, & \u00fea \u00fe\u00e6r gearn mycel m\u00e6nio to him\n\u00d0a w\u00e6s heora sum re\u00f0ra & hatheortra \u00feonne \u00fea o\u00f0re w\u00e6ron, & se \u00f0a gebr\u00e6gd his sweorde & mynte\n\u00dea he, sanctus Martinus, \u00fe\u00e6t geseah, \u00fea dyde he sona \u00fe\u00e6t hr\u00e6gel of his sweoran, & leat for\u00f0 to \u00feam\n\u00d0a he \u00f0a, se h\u00e6\u00f0ena man, upprihte mid his handa & hine sclean sceolde, \u00fea feoll he f\u00e6ringa on\nAc he w\u00e6s mid godcunde egesan swi\u00f0e ge\u00feread, & he \u00fea him \u00feone eadigan wer, sancte Martine,\nSwylce w\u00e6s eft eac o\u00f0er wundor \u00feyssum onlic, & \u00fe\u00e6t gelamp sume si\u00f0e \u00fe\u00e6r he sum deofulgild br\u00e6c\n\u00dea br\u00e6gd \u00feara h\u00e6\u00f0enra manna sum his seax.\n\u00dea se h\u00e6\u00f0ena man hine stingan wolde, \u00fea nyste he f\u00e6ringa hw\u00e6r \u00fe\u00e6t seax cwom \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00e6r on handa\nGelomlice \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feonne w\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6r he \u00f0a idlan gild br\u00e6c & him \u00fea h\u00e6\u00f0enan men wi\u00feerwearde w\u00e6ron, \u00fe\u00e6t\n& he to \u00fe\u00e6s mihtig w\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00e6lce untrumnesse to h\u00e6lanne, & to \u00fe\u00e6s mycle gife he \u00f0\u00e6s \u00e6t Gode\nGe \u00fe\u00e6t oft gelamp \u00feonne hwylc man his hr\u00e6gles d\u00e6l to untrumum menn brohte \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00feonne \u00feurh\nIn \u00feyssum he \u00feonne w\u00e6s ealles swi\u00f0ost to herigenne, \u00fe\u00e6t he n\u00e6fre n\u00e6nigum woruldricum men ne\nAc hie a in eallum so\u00f0 & riht don wolde.\n\u00deis is so\u00f0lice eadig wer, ne w\u00e6s n\u00e6fre facen ne inwit in his heortan, ne \u00e6nigne unrihtlice demde nene\nNe hine \u00e6nig man yrre ne gramheortne ne geseah, ac he w\u00e6s in anum mode, & efne heofonlice blisse\n& ne gehyrde \u00e6nig man aht elles of his mu\u00f0e butan Cristes lof & nytte spr\u00e6ce, ne aht elles on his\nSwylce eac \u00fees eadiga wer, sanctus Martinus, mycle \u00e6r beforan \u00fee he \u00feone d\u00e6g wisse his for\u00f0si\u00f0e, &\n& he \u00fea his bro\u00f0rum s\u00e6gde \u00fe\u00e6t hit \u00fea \u00e6trihte w\u00e6re \u00fe\u00e6t he of \u00feisse worulde sceolde.\n\u00d0a wiste he sumne hired on his bisceopscire \u00fea \u00fee unge\u00feweare & ungesybsume him betweonum\n\u00dea ferde he \u00feyder mid his \u00feegnum, \u00feeah \u00f0e he wiste \u00fe\u00e6t hit \u00fea \u00e6t his dea\u00f0d\u00e6ge w\u00e6re, \u00fe\u00e6t he huru\n\u00dea cwomon hie to sumre ea, \u00fea gesawon hie \u00feara wel feala \u00feara fugela \u00fee we scealfras nemna\u00fe, & hie\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 sanctus Martinus: Hw\u00e6t, \u00feas wiht habba\u00f0 deofla onlicnesse, swa \u00fee deofol a s\u00e6ta\u00fe hw\u00e6r he\n\u00d0a bebead sanctus Martinus \u00feam fugelum \u00fe\u00e6t hie \u00feanon fram \u00feam w\u00e6tere gewiten, & on westen &\n& efne on \u00fea gelicnesse swa he \u00feone deoful of stowa gehwylcre geflymde \u00fe\u00e6r he \u00feonne w\u00e6s, swa \u00f0a\n& hie \u00fe\u00e6t wundredon \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6t gesawon & his fera w\u00e6ron \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0a fugelas sylfe eac sancte Martine\n\u00d0a he \u00fea h\u00e6fde \u00feone hyred gesybbodne \u00fee he \u00fe\u00e6r to ferde, & \u00fe\u00e6r well manige dagas w\u00e6s, & \u00fea he \u00f0a\n\u00dea het he ealle his \u00feegnas him to, & he him s\u00e6gde \u00fe\u00e6t he for\u00f0feran sceolde.\n\u00dea weopon hie ealle sona, & sarlice geb\u00e6rdon for heora hlaforde, & hie \u00feus cw\u00e6don to him: For hwan\nO\u00f0\u00f0e hwam bebeodest \u00f0u us eac gif \u00f0u gewitest?\nCuma\u00fe rixiende wulfas & todrifa\u00fe \u00feine heorde.\nHwa forstande\u00f0 \u00feonne hie gif \u00f0u hie ne scyldest?\nWe \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feonne witan \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t is \u00feines modes willa \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0u mote \u00feas woruld forl\u00e6tan & Crist geseon.\nAc miltsa \u00f0u \u00feonne hw\u00e6\u00f0re us & gemyne ure \u00feearfe.\n\u00d0a he \u00f0a heora spr\u00e6ce \u00feyllice gehyrde & he hie ealle wepende geseah, \u00fea weop he sylfa eac, & his\nW\u00e6s he to \u00fe\u00e6s arf\u00e6st \u00fe\u00e6t him w\u00e6s \u00e6g\u00f0er on weorce, ge \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00f0a bro\u00f0or forlete, ge huru \u00feone \u00fe\u00e6t\nHw\u00e6t, we nu gehyra\u00fe, men \u00fea leofestan, hu haliglice \u00fees eadiga wer, sanctus Martinus, his lif for\nAnd nu a \u00f0a hwile \u00fee \u00feeos world stande\u00f0, his go\u00f0 man m\u00e6rsa\u00f0 geond ealne middangeard in Godes\n& he nu mid eallum halgum a to widan feore in heofona rice for dryhtnes onsyne gefyh\u00f0 & blissa\u00fe.\nAc utan we la tilian, men \u00fea leofestan, \u00fe\u00e6t we \u00fe\u00e6s halgan weres, sanctus Martinus, lif & his d\u00e6da\nDryhten us to \u00feam gefultumige se \u00f0e leofa\u00fe & rixa\u00fe aa in eallra worulda world a butan ende, amen.",
